      "text": "To find the midpoint of a segment with given endpoints, we use the midpoint formula:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} \\right) \\]\nwhere $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ are the coordinates of the endpoints.\n\nGiven endpoints are $(6, 12)$ and $(0, -6)$, we can substitute these values into the formula:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{6 + 0}{2}, \\frac{12 + (-6)}{2} \\right) \\]\nSimplifying the coordinates, we get:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{6}{2}, \\frac{6}{2} \\right) \\]\n\\[ \\left( 3, 3 \\right) \\]\n\nThe sum of the coordinates of the midpoint is:\n\\[ 3 + 3 = 6 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the coordinates of the midpoint is $\\boxed{6}$.",
